+## 2026-10-22 PostgreSQL admission-schema proposal
+
+`S13_POSTGRES_ADMISSION_SCHEMA_DESIGN_2026-10-22.md` now proposes representing the existing S12 `PERMITTED → DISPATCHED` CAS as one durable dispatch-attempt identity, with process binding and monotonic physical-call progress. It explicitly rejects a second admission authorization source and keeps the lifecycle epoch authoritative. The proposal also defines the durable recovery-barrier snapshot, but it has no migration or adapter implementation and has not completed database, reliability, security, or exact GPT-PM review. It changes no S13 gate or readiness state.
+
+## 2026-10-22 S13 lock-protocol review correction
+
+PM Bridge request `c9b13d91-4b2c-4d4c-9d4a-98eac51fe352` returned a correlated `REVISE` for attachment SHA-256 `2500FFD7A45A4A53390D8B73FFC3D297F662BC4AC43B0418639D2EF6E461D4C0`, but its envelope identified project `ERP` and repository `D:\Repo\ERP`, not `ERP_MCP`. The reply ID was `bf60ebe8-8f37-5c1e-a2e5-50166ce7a898`. It is not an ERP_MCP approval or a commit gate. Its four findings were checked against the named local ERP_MCP sources and corrected in the current scope-fence, admission, and adapter-error designs: require `READ COMMITTED`; order actual hashed advisory resources with deduplication; keep non-locking lifecycle checks before the lifecycle row-lock rank and revalidate at that rank; and map only a dedicated bounded fence timeout to `LEDGER_LOCK_TIMEOUT`.
+
+For follow-up request `6f70e13f-a1ab-47e4-adb0-b4e9b207b21d` (intermediate patch hash `805CC5CE3E2EF47F7FE850DD6CC841916D74FB771A2AEA0F2AF000CF8ADE0F21`), persisted PM Bridge job status reports `uncertain` / `CHATGPT_SEND_UNCONFIRMED`, with no `userTurnId` or `replyId`. The correlated response to current request `d9f2bb82-5519-4d7c-9a8e-8b8c8b907a31` (attachment SHA-256 `7F18293E6609B86406525BE3C2D55531EEFE8CF28D5E7FA36691B70A479F5372`) asserts that the earlier hash was approved, but the response supplies no prior reply ID and conflicts with that persisted job record. Therefore the earlier approval claim remains **UNVERIFIED** and does not authorize a commit. The current exact-patch response is correlated `REVISE`, with 0 BLOCKER, 2 MAJOR, 0 MINOR, and 1 INFO; it is not commit-ready. Its MAJOR findings are addressed in this revision by recording the conflicting provenance without promoting either claim to approval, and by including the linked detail record in the exact review patch. This revised package still requires fresh exact-hash review.
+
+The local code-reviewer pass found no lock-order contradiction in the namespace-7/rank correction and confirmed the existing namespace-2-to-5 kill-switch/sweep edge from migration 020. It found one minor lesson-log drift, now corrected to distinguish namespace-5 sweep, namespace-6 global IDs, and namespace-7 scope-fence collision behavior. These are static reviews only; the proposed protocol is not implemented or runtime-qualified.
+
