+# Change record: make the S13 lock protocol fail closed on PostgreSQL lock errors
+
+Date: 2026-10-22  
+Scope: S13 lock ordering and stable refusal-code contract; a generic Python error-mapping change plus design documentation. The runtime transaction isolation/fence protocol is not implemented here.
+
+## What changed
+
+- Removed the global mapping from PostgreSQL SQLSTATE `55P03` to `LEDGER_LOCK_TIMEOUT`; raw `55P03` now remains `SQL_55P03` unless a dedicated SQL helper raises the explicit contract code.
+- Updated the S13 scope-fence and admission designs to require a fresh top-level `READ COMMITTED` transaction, with isolation set before any SQL that can establish a snapshot.
+- Defined lock ordering on actual advisory-lock integer keys: derive, deduplicate, and sort the acquired integer resources within each namespace rank. This covers hash collisions for namespace 6 and existing multi-key namespaces 2–4.
+- Preserved namespace 5 after source inspection found migration 020 already uses it for recovery-sweep serialization; assigned namespace 7 to the new scope fence. The rank now includes the existing switch-to-sweep edge before global-ID locks.
